        "header": "2Related Work",
        "images": [
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.30222/2609.30222v1/te_arch_sep2.png",
                "caption": "Figure 2:TrackEverything architecture.TrackEverything processes videos in sliding windows of lengthLL.Encoding:Video frames are encoded and unprojected into a world-coordinate 3D feature cloud using depths/pointmaps from sensors or geometry predictors.Endpoint Refinement:Conditioned on source/target position embeddings and 3D WAFT feature sampling, a recurrent transformer iteratively predicts each point’s 3D offsetΔ​𝐱\\Delta\\mathbf{x}at the target timestep, visibility, and a static/dynamic classification.Trajectory Refinement:Trajectories for dynamic points are initialized via constant-velocity interpolation and refined via within-track temporal self-attention and cross-attention from track summary tokens ([cls]) to the scene cloud.Output and De-duplication:At window boundaries, points arriving at identical 3D voxels are merged by mean-pooling before initializing the subsequent window, bounding representation size across long videos.",
                "position": 386
            }
        ]
